REPAIRAGENT-OCI THOUGHTS: [0m The focused range confirms the run path handles poststart hook failures differently from prestart/create hooks: prestart/create use `ret != 0`, while poststart uses `ret < 0`. Since `do_hooks` can return a nonzero hook exit status (e.g. `/bin/false` returns 1), the poststart failure is ignored. The next step is to patch this exact condition, with an explanatory comment, so any nonzero poststart hook result becomes fatal like the other OCI hook stages.
